WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.668
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:04.670
and comedian you know
from "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.172
which premieres
this Saturday on NBC and Peacock

00:00:07.172 --> 00:00:10.710
with host Pete Davidson
and musical guest Ice Spice.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.446
He also stars in
"Dicks: The Musical,"

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:16.115
which is in select theaters
now and nationwide October 20th.

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:17.216
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:19.052
our very good friend Bowen Yang,
everybody.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.353
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:33.967 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.669
Welcome back.
-Thank you. Thanks, Seth.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.137
-You have not just "SNL."

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:40.940
You have one of my favorite
podcasts, "Las Culturistas."

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.375
-Oh, my goodness.
-And you took it on --

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.276
[ Cheers and applause ]
There we go. Give it up.

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:46.713
-You know, someone might
be on it soon.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:49.815
-I can't wait.
You took it to Europe.

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:53.419
You did live shows in London
and Berlin and Amsterdam.

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:54.620
-Yes, yes.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.423
Those are the big
expat markets, apparently.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.526
-Yeah.
-It was really fun.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:01.127
-We talked about Amsterdam.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.495
I was doing shows
in Amsterdam in the summer.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:03.596
I went back to Boom Chicago,

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.031
which is the theater
I used to work at.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.167
And it's actually where
you did your live podcast.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.634
-That's right, that's right.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.069
-Did you do anything fun in
Amsterdam while you were there?

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.871
-We just walked the canals.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.374
We took a boat,
and I love Amsterdam.

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:17.043
I went twice this summer.
I -- My only issue with it

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:20.647
is that it's tough
when you combine a city --

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:24.117
when you combine weed
with bicycles.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:27.120
I feel like it's a recipe
for disaster.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.421
Crossing the street
is really scary.

00:01:29.421 --> 00:01:30.690
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.425
It is not -- So you even --

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.227
You're not even saying
like being on a bicycle,

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.929
just being stoned
on foot is scary

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:38.831
because there's so many
bicycles.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.399
-You don't have to be
the person who's stoned.

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:42.835
You might be next
to a stoned person,

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.971
and then they're the ones
who, like, causes a big,

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.507
like 10-person pileup
or something.

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.241
-A bike pileup.
-A bike pileup.

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:51.677
-It is. I will say,
you have to do a lot wrong

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:53.913
for a car to come near you
on a bicycle in Amsterdam.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.181
Like, the cars
are so aware of the bikes,

00:01:56.181 --> 00:01:58.384
and that is very nice.
But I will say on foot,

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:00.186
sometimes you'll just walk
right into the path.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.220
-That's right, that's right.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.721
-And the Dutch people
are very --

00:02:02.721 --> 00:02:05.358
I love them very much.
They are cold and unforgiving.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.693
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:09.729
-But that said with love.
-Yes.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.064
Did you go to did you go
to any museums?

00:02:12.064 --> 00:02:15.734
-I did. The hot ticket
is the Van Gogh Museum,

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:16.970
and concierge in my hotel

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.904
was very, very good
about getting me tickets.

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:21.173
And he did say to me,

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:25.444
"This is harder than getting
Taylor Swift tickets."

00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:27.780
And I said,
"That can't be true."

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.216
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.485
There's no way that's true."
And, like, you know,

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.687
there aren't, like, teen girls
fighting me for it,

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.422
so it's fine.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:40.192
-There was I feel like a fight
to get into the Lincoln Center,

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:42.395
Las Culturistas Awards.
-Yes.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:44.029
-You did that this --
Was it this summer?

00:02:44.029 --> 00:02:46.265
-It was this summer, yes.
-And so one of our producers,

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:49.302
Henry, was there, and he said
there was literally two loops

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.670
around the block to get in.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.371
-Yeah, that's pretty crazy.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.473
It was a free show.
So that explains it.

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:55.641
-Yeah. Yeah. Free show.

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:57.443
But again, you were
giving out awards

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.011
and they were
the culture awards.

00:02:59.011 --> 00:02:59.946
-That's right.
-And for people

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.047
who don't know the podcast,

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.115
you kind of give out
the sort of awards

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:04.216
that I feel like are overlooked

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:05.785
by a lot of
the main award shows.

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.119
-Absolutely.
-Like, for example,

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:10.356
you gave out the the Chris Award
for Most Timeless Name.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.825
-Most Timeless Name.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:17.330
-The nominees were John,
Jess, George, Mark and Doja.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:21.500
-Yeah, Doja. Doja Cat. Pretty
timeless name, I would say.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.335
She did not win.
-Do you remember who won?

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:24.571
-Oh, this is a quiz.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.172
-No, I didn't mean
to make it a quiz.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:27.306
-That's okay.
-I was going to say it.

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:28.608
-Please.
-Jess.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:30.877
-Jess.
-And why do you think --

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:32.645
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:34.213
-I don't know.

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:36.315
This is literally
on a spreadsheet

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:39.685
and we just, like,
change the cell color to blue.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:42.555
We're like, "Yeah, this one.
Let's crown it."

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.390
-This is my favorite --
Free Willy Award

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.893
for Animal Achievement,
Jenny the donkey.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.728
-Oh, from
"Banshees of Inisherin."

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.463
-Had a big year.
Mickey Mouse.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.565
Always good year.
-Big year for Mickey.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.801
-The cast
of "The Secret Life of Pets,"

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.502
which I feel like
came out a while ago.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:04:00.572
-Right.
But look, they've achieved.

00:04:00.572 --> 00:04:04.143
-And then the winner
was tortoises, all.

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:07.146
-All tortoises.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:09.048
-I mean, it does --
it makes sense

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.616
people were lined
around the block.

00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:12.919
-Yes. You want to know.

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:14.087
You want to know.
There were big upsets.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:16.021
I mean, Jenny the donkey
is probably really upset.

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:17.957
-I know. Jenny looked
at the nominees and was like,

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.159
"It's my year."
-"It's my year," but no.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.660
-The good news for Jenny is
based on

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.962
"The Secret Life of Pets" cast,

00:04:23.962 --> 00:04:26.398
Jenny might get nominated
10 years from now.

00:04:26.398 --> 00:04:27.666
-Definitely, definitely.

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:28.701
-Don't give up.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.269
-If Colin Farrell
can make a comeback,

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:32.305
so can Jenny.
-Yeah, that's true.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:34.240
Pete Davidson
is hosting this week.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.042
-Yes!
-Now that must be the first time

00:04:37.042 --> 00:04:38.810
someone you worked with
has come back to host.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:40.045
Is that --
-Yeah. That's true.

00:04:40.045 --> 00:04:42.915
-That's a real passage of time.
I think maybe --

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.350
Well, probably for me
it was Will Ferrell.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.851
Will Ferrell came back to host
and I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:04:45.851 --> 00:04:47.185
We were cast members together."

00:04:47.185 --> 00:04:49.989
And so what has it been like
for you with Pete back?

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:51.524
-It's been great.
It's so nice.

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:54.394
It's just nice to like have the
shorthand already with someone.

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:55.427
-Yeah.

00:04:55.427 --> 00:04:56.529
-And we did our read-through
yesterday

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.998
and he -- we read
about like 35 sketches.

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:02.502
Right? And I think at the half,
at the break he said,

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:04.637
"This is more sketches
than I've been in

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.572
than my eight years
at this show."

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.374
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.409
We were like,
"Maybe you're right."

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:11.877
-Five months out of the office.

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:14.647
Now, I guess you got a little --
you lost some shows on

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.315
the back end of the season,

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:18.083
but it was the summer
when people are away.

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:19.986
But, you know,
it was abbreviated year,

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:21.353
and maybe people left
a little bit quicker

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:22.855
than they would have.
What was the scene

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.457
like as everybody
went back to their offices?

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:26.191
-It was smelly.
-Yeah.

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:28.995
-It was smelly
because five months,

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:33.933
guess what's in the fridges.
Our takeout food from May.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:37.402
-Yeah.
-And yeah, I think,

00:05:37.402 --> 00:05:40.773
I still have a fruit cup
in my fridge down the hall

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:45.244
that has the whitest and
blackest mold I've ever seen.

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.645
-That's amazing.
-That's amazing.

00:05:46.645 --> 00:05:48.614
-You know what? You don't just
do comedy, you do science.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.316
And that's what I've always
respected about you.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.018
I want to talk about
"Dicks: The Musical."

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:54.253
We'll be right back with more
from Bowen Yang.

